## Summary

Adds loopback HTTP integration coverage using the actual `WorkspaceProjectHTTPServer`, real `WorkspaceService` / `ProjectService`, a provider-neutral fake `WorkspaceStore`, and fake authentication/authorization adapters that return the real security contracts.

Coverage includes:
- 401 authentication failure and 403 permission denial;
- workspace-list authorization filtering before pagination, with bounded cursor/limit behavior;
- workspace update/archive lifecycle and permission mapping;
- project register/read/list/replace/unregister lifecycle using canonical `ProjectManifest` payloads and project resource refs;
- denial and explicit authorization-service unavailability before malformed body parsing, with store call-count assertions proving no mutation occurs;
- stable 400s for invalid list bounds/cursors, mutation query parameters, unknown body fields and path/body project-id mismatch;
- stable 404/409 mapping for missing resources and archived-workspace mutation conflicts;
- stable JSON 405 on a known route with an unsupported method.

## Evidence boundary

This PR changes tests only. It does not run or qualify the concrete OIDC/store-authoritative RBAC/audit composition, and no exact-head CI/release qualification is claimed.

## Scope

