## Summary
Implements GP-17.9 with an evidence-driven testnet onboarding qualification gate.

### Qualification binding
- exact canonical game ID;
- exact application ID;
- discovered `testnet` environment;
- discovered testnet chain ID;
- exact 40-character lowercase commit SHA;
- live-network observation timestamp and evidence.

### Required evidence
- network discovery;
- testnet developer-account/faucet access;
- SDK integration;
- canonical registration read;
- finalized state read under GP-16 semantics;
- wallet-free core / optional wallet linkage;
- exact game/action authority scope.

Missing required evidence yields BLOCKED; explicit failures yield FAIL. Only a complete live-network evidence set yields `QUALIFIED_FOR_TESTNET_ONBOARDING`.

Developer Hub remains noncanonical: this creates no Registry registration or CapabilityRegistry grant and is not a security certification. Repository CI and GP-17.8 local/devnet rehearsal cannot manufacture live-testnet qualification.

Roadmap marks GP-17.8 complete through PR #262 and GP-17.9 in qualification. GP-17.10 developer UX/docs/closeout follows after exact-head qualification and merge.

## Summary

Repairs a structural evidence-integrity gap in MAA-7/8 without modifying the stable API, production routing, numerical kernels, or concurrent FDAL work.

The previous constructors compared cardinalities, not candidate membership or the route that generated the oracle. A Boolean mask admitting {0,2} could be paired with relabeled survivor IDs {1,3} while keeping all count checks green. The new guards fail closed for this substitution.

Changes:
- retain an immutable qualification-route snapshot, recomposition policy, and the first nonidentity candidate-to-Boolean-block mapping in SurvivorSet; general batches still support arbitrary IDs;
- validate the exact route, full M13B signature/mask/schema/generation metadata, candidate mapping including rejected candidates, complete bounded candidate geometry, actual Boolean control cardinality and every surviving candidate's mask membership;
- enforce realizable set-intersection counts and nested-reference coverage lower bounds;
- require latency minima/maxima to be observed extrema, including singleton/two-sample constraints and full u64 boundary safety;
- preserve existing tests and add 13 integration regressions, including exhaustive 4,096 four-bit matched records, independently enumerated set intersections and sample sequences, metadata substitutions, candidate relabeling and the 63/64 bit boundary;
- add read-only exact-head maa-host CI with Rust 1.89, formatting, strict Clippy, debug/release tests and strict docs;
- update README and the MAA roadmap; document the remaining numerical harness, provenance and GPU gates.

## Validation observed before PR creation

Branch preparation at 59a206d03cebebe56ff6e26d903b3864843ae567 passed cargo fmt, Clippy -D warnings, 53 unit tests and 13 integration tests on GitHub Actions run 34894528242. The temporary branch-scoped preparation workflow was removed before this PR; it is not part of the resulting diff. No local Rust execution is claimed. The final PR head must independently pass maa-host and all existing applicable CI/WGPU/CodeQL/semver/supply-chain gates before merge.

## Explicit limits

This is bounded host correctness qualification, not numerical attention quality or a speedup. The route snapshot is not a cryptographic attestation of Q/K/V or predicate definitions. Workload identifiers, dense relevance labels and latency observations remain caller-supplied. Sample-count equality alone does not prove matched hardware, warmup or timing scope. Future experiments must distinguish block-level candidate accounting from executed scalar Q.K work and physical traffic.

The existing hourly Research Autopilot remains the recurring continuation mechanism; this PR introduces no separate scheduler.

Prefer squash merge after exact-head green checks so the branch-only preparation history is not added to main.

## Summary

Audits the current manuscript against `Ae4_Article_Corrected(2).zip`, using the corrected 2018 `Saliva.tex`, `mybib.bib` and reviewer reply as the primary historical record.

### Scientific corrections and additions

- restores the acinar then ductal two-stage framing and states explicitly that the model addresses primary acinar secretion rather than final duct-modified saliva;
- restores the historical NKCC1 evidence and the bicarbonate-dependent residual chloride-loading motivation;
- records that the 2018 model predicted only minimal NKCC1 compensation after AE loss;
- adds the important experimental tension between the 2015 isolated NKCC1/NHE assays and the strong integrated NKCC1 compensation in Task 40;
- makes clear that the Task 40 compensation is a model prediction requiring direct testing, not an experimentally established AE4-null response;
- adds a dedicated Scope and limitations subsection covering compartment scope, prescribed calcium, simplified beta regulation, imported/surrogate transporter kinetics, structural NBC interpretation, Task 42 inherited kinetics, Task 41 target selection and the 600 s validation horizon;
- expands the claims and evidence ledger accordingly.

### Bibliography

Merges the current manuscript bibliography with the corrected 2018 archive bibliography into 56 unique entries. Seven duplicate legacy keys are collapsed onto the current manuscript keys. The merge also corrects the Peña 2015 author metadata, the garbled Imai 1973 author list, several incorrect legacy DOI fields, and a set of verified missing DOI fields.

A detailed provenance record is added at `manuscript/corrected_archive_audit.md`.

### Scientific state

No model source, frozen trajectory, simulation checkpoint, figure source value or numerical result is changed by this PR.

